From 40f82c28e05e571ae9c1e05f7ca6449a1c6dbd9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lakitu12 <1219387824@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:35:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 61/63] um: qcow2: a read/write engine for the ubd backend

Boot qcow2 images directly: reads decompress deflate clusters, writes
allocate clusters and maintain the L2 and refcount accounting, so the
image stays sparse wherever the guest has not written.  Format
authority is qemu's docs/interop/qcow2.txt (fetched from the v10.0.0
tag); every layout constant cites the spec.

Refused with a reason at open: backing files, snapshots (read-only),
external data files, encryption, extended L2 entries, zstd compression,
refcount widths other than 16-bit, cluster sizes outside 512..64K.

The engine is host-side UML code: it parses in kernel context at open
and does I/O on the ubd helper thread, where only os_* syscall wrappers
and the preallocated arena may be touched -- no allocation, no printk,
no locks outside open.  Crash ordering favours leaks (repairable by
qemu-img check) over dangling references.  Inflate comes from a
vendored, allocation-free tinfl (miniz 3.0.2, MIT, license text kept).

The host selftest caught the one subtlety worth spelling out for
reviewers: bit 0 is the zero flag only on standard descriptors; on
compressed entries it is part of the offset.
